description: 'Design the structured concurrency model for Jinn (review 12_safety,
  P1-16 adjacent). Current state: docs/concurrency.md is the canonical shutdown contract
  (scheduler runtime/sched.c, channels runtime/channel.c, actor lowering src/codegen/actors.rs)
  and is test-backed by tests/concurrency_shutdown.rs. Missing: no scope/nursery construct
  — actors/coroutines are not bound to a lexical scope that joins children on exit.
  Deliverable: a design doc (docs/structured-concurrency.md) defining scope syntax
  (idiomatic Jinn prose-style), child lifetime rules, cancellation propagation, error
  propagation from children (interacts with locked error model in docs/error-effects.md),
  and how `stop`/`close` compose with scopes. Definition of done: doc reviewed and
  consistent with existing shutdown semantics + error model.'
